Clinical Course: The distorted vision will not improve on its own and requires specialized injections into the eye by a specialist to stop the leaking vessels and attempt to preserve your central sight.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Go to the Emergency Department immediately if your eye suddenly becomes intensely painful, or if it feels like a dark curtain is dropping over your entire field of vision. You must attend the urgent eye specialist appointment tomorrow morning.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The "dry" wear and tear in the back of your eye has suddenly turned "wet," meaning tiny abnormal blood vessels have started leaking fluid under the center of your vision. This fluid acts like a blister, physically warping the retina and making straight lines look bent. The eye specialist has injections that can seal these leaks.
Actionable Steps: Lightly patch the bad eye tonight if the distortion is making you dizzy or off-balance when walking. Do not attempt to drive. Attend your urgent specialist appointment first thing tomorrow.

